{"name":"Modesty","hex":"#d4c7d9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"modesty","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The quality of being modest; having a limited and not overly high opinion of oneself and one's abilities.","Moderate behaviour; reserve."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modesty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Modesty","blocks":[{"text":"Modesty, sometimes known as demureness, is a mode of dress and deportment which intends to avoid the encouraging of sexual attraction in others. The word modesty comes from the Latin word modestus which means 'keeping within measure'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/CaliforniaBeachc1905.jpg/330px-CaliforniaBeachc1905.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modesty","wikidata":"Q11199149"},{"title":"Modesty (Corradini sculpture)","blocks":[{"text":"Modesty or Chastity or Veiled Truth by Antonio Corradini is a sculpture completed in 1752 during the Rococo period. Raimondo di Sangro commissioned Corradini to sculpt a memorial for his mother in the Cappella Sansevero in Naples, where the marble sculpture still stands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Pudicizia%2C_Cappella_Sansevero.jpg/330px-Pudicizia%2C_Cappella_Sansevero.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modesty_(Corradini_sculpture)","wikidata":"Q30908922"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/1868-skirt-lengths-girl-ages-Harpers-Bazar.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/1868-skirt-lengths-girl-ages-Harpers-Bazar.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"1868 diagram from Harper's Bazaar showing proper girls' skirt lengths i